  'Introduction to Social Work',
  'Students learn social work''s professional purpose, values, and scope, then place the profession in historical context and practice person-in-environment and generalist thinking across micro, mezzo, and macro levels. Topics cover ethics and professional judgment, cultural humility, human rights and advocacy, social welfare systems, fields of practice, engagement, assessment and resource navigation, evidence-informed practice, trauma-informed care, organizations and community practice, education and licensure, and a reflective field-exploration portfolio.',
  $iswjson${"slug": "introduction-to-social-work", "title": "Introduction to Social Work", "description": "Students learn social work's professional purpose, values, and scope, then place the profession in historical context and practice person-in-environment and generalist thinking across micro, mezzo, and macro levels. Topics cover ethics and professional judgment, cultural humility, human rights and advocacy, social welfare systems, fields of practice, engagement, assessment and resource navigation, evidence-informed practice, trauma-informed care, organizations and community practice, education and licensure, and a reflective field-exploration portfolio.", "topics": [{"id": "c70687e3-24b2-4f39-9802-582014d6ce8f", "type": "topic", "title": "Professional Purpose, Scope, and Social Work Values", "description": "Added for comprehensive coverage", "children": [{"id": "b41bf217-f95d-4d2b-814e-c65dcdb03dfe", "type": "subtopic", "title": "What social work is", "children": [{"id": "4fa39e40-7214-4c1f-85ee-ca56839b4116", "type": "concept", "title": "Professional mission"}, {"id": "4e9afbf9-c2f7-4a57-8bde-dd67d7032e2a", "type": "concept", "title": "Service, social justice, dignity and worth, importance of relationships, integrity, and competence"}, {"id": "9e4d363f-4cad-41bf-9ffb-ecd2f1da59fa", "type": "concept", "title": "Helping roles across direct practice, policy, and community work"}, {"id": "95b9d0fd-e294-482e-8146-3433b6220562", "type": "concept", "title": "Distinctions from psychology, counseling, sociology, public health, and criminal justice"}], "description": "Students learn the profession's purpose: helping people and communities improve wellbeing while challenging conditions that create harm."}, {"id": "fd5dedf9-f526-4134-a031-3dbc2220eab8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Professional identity and public purpose", "children": [{"id": "78aeefe1-a0d3-4000-aba0-2e09c5742590", "type": "concept", "title": "Person-in-environment orientation"}, {"id": "d061a21c-257d-4cd5-aef8-3b12bc257c2c", "type": "concept", "title": "Human rights and social justice commitments"}, {"id": "47f24601-873c-4052-8770-b0a49d89bd12", "type": "concept", "title": "Strengths and empowerment perspectives"}, {"id": "7e57fd2f-b93c-4204-9d2b-892a7a234c11", "type": "concept", "title": "Accountability to clients, communities, agencies, and the profession"}], "description": "This subtopic frames social work as a values-driven profession with public responsibilities, not simply a set of helping techniques."}, {"id": "afef8413-4e15-4edd-b8f9-2b284f511fe1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Scope of practice and professional settings", "children": [{"id": "166476c7-1361-4ede-b5cc-90fec8f60721", "type": "concept", "title": "Clinical, school, medical, child welfare, aging, behavioral health, community, policy, and administrative roles"}, {"id": "52f20c5e-ad56-40ee-83ee-1f8f19be765f", "type": "concept", "title": "Voluntary and involuntary service contexts"}, {"id": "d816576d-8605-4eaa-b3aa-744d5c66caf5", "type": "concept", "title": "Public, nonprofit, private, and community-based practice"}, {"id": "c51dafe1-578a-4c1a-bb37-c035d8c01e6f", "type": "concept", "title": "Specialization after generalist foundations"}], "description": "Students begin to see how varied social work roles can be while still sharing a common foundation."}]}, {"id": "a4d289e7-a060-4795-b010-2f1d2361de16", "type": "topic", "title": "History of Social Work and Social Welfare", "description": "This topic places the profession in historical context, from mutual aid and settlement houses to modern social services and policy debates.", "children": [{"id": "cbe7dc21-e191-47ce-bd0e-59a7ad6f3695", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Mutual aid, charity, and settlement traditions", "children": [{"id": "69f1c88f-e07a-4ded-83ff-f05d030eebfb", "type": "concept", "title": "Mutual aid and community care"}, {"id": "539a39ee-c588-4a00-a302-4697127d2acf", "type": "concept", "title": "Charity organization societies"}, {"id": "ea57149a-8f72-47a3-9b4c-4dd221c44299", "type": "concept", "title": "Settlement-house movement"}, {"id": "98591df5-0cf5-472f-b265-7847883a764e", "type": "concept", "title": "Mary Richmond, Jane Addams, and contested professional roots"}], "description": "The field's history helps students understand present debates about poverty, deservingness, charity, solidarity, and reform."}, {"id": "a7b46eb6-046c-40fe-877c-d843c36c2091", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Professionalization and social welfare institutions", "children": [{"id": "050477de-b412-436a-b92a-fe90cb51999c", "type": "concept", "title": "Early casework and group work"}, {"id": "f8755304-0dd9-4ae3-8dce-1a6a69c0ef07", "type": "concept", "title": "New Deal and Great Society expansions"}, {"id": "0b8947cc-7311-4a27-a9e5-4978b477c128", "type": "concept", "title": "Mental health, child welfare, aging, and disability services"}, {"id": "0f9cbf87-ac53-48cf-b0f1-47fdfe358be7", "type": "concept", "title": "CSWE accreditation and social work education"}], "description": "Students trace how social work became a profession linked to agencies, universities, licensing, ethics, and public policy."}, {"id": "c9172a8c-e55f-4c4a-b4a2-331d2dfce18e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Critical history and unfinished justice", "children": [{"id": "08f09ec7-1f38-4334-8755-9ad2882980a1", "type": "concept", "title": "Racism, colonialism, eugenics, and family regulation"}, {"id": "d93b8468-553d-4b97-8905-028c3fb48ea4", "type": "concept", "title": "Segregated services and discriminatory policy"}, {"id": "49720bcd-e7b3-4e5d-89b0-3de8589eb679", "type": "concept", "title": "Community resistance and social movements"}, {"id": "57cd7160-b274-4397-9c91-638506ad21aa", "type": "concept", "title": "Contemporary reform, abolition, and transformation debates"}], "description": "A comprehensive introduction names both the profession's contributions and its participation in coercive or exclusionary systems."}]}, {"id": "e1994b24-c2b6-4da6-8479-9ffacb613e4a", "type": "topic", "title": "Person-in-Environment, Systems Thinking, and Human Behavior", "description": "Students learn the central social work habit of seeing people, families, groups, organizations, communities, policy, and culture together.", "children": [{"id": "992223f9-4b32-4884-9145-3ec8d4c28124", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Person-in-environment perspective", "children": [{"id": "3ac76913-8b1d-48c6-b7c2-e4fdce455166", "type": "concept", "title": "Biological, psychological, social, spiritual, and cultural dimensions"}, {"id": "ff81d177-a391-4024-8374-c3fd4aecb411", "type": "concept", "title": "Family, peer, school, work, neighborhood, and policy environments"}, {"id": "28ec1262-da09-4495-b843-fe14e1693b5e", "type": "concept", "title": "Risk and protective factors"}, {"id": "23ed3eb0-bf19-41ae-bd98-9556bb9f18e7", "type": "concept", "title": "Ecological assessment"}], "description": "Students learn to connect individual experience to relationships, institutions, communities, policy, and culture."}, {"id": "719b50ed-38ad-4781-9cb1-4a634e7c9899", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Systems and ecological thinking", "children": [{"id": "28bd48ab-8a58-455d-b5d2-977cf728c16e", "type": "concept", "title": "Micro, mezzo, exo, and macro systems"}, {"id": "b0b1f6af-769a-48db-baaa-7f78a51f01a2", "type": "concept", "title": "Feedback loops and reciprocal influence"}, {"id": "64f28b51-226e-4b7c-9963-96396cd56a1a", "type": "concept", "title": "Organizations and communities as social environments"}, {"id": "995f9146-0dab-4dc1-a25b-1c937f4ff66f", "type": "concept", "title": "Fit between people and environments"}], "description": "Systems thinking prevents simplistic explanations and helps students locate leverage points for change."}, {"id": "aa5bcf3d-ed0e-420e-b370-d7858178e295", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Development, resilience, and life course", "children": [{"id": "bd0cef23-b378-430a-83cd-1147cf78a859", "type": "concept", "title": "Lifespan development"}, {"id": "fe2ca846-8b03-46f3-b166-b016cebc68ff", "type": "concept", "title": "Attachment, stress, coping, and resilience"}, {"id": "79464f31-e6a8-47a1-9b7c-e8db0b832564", "type": "concept", "title": "Trauma and adverse childhood experiences"}, {"id": "01442563-b821-4262-9469-03a7c11d6a47", "type": "concept", "title": "Aging, disability, caregiving, and life transitions"}], "description": "Human behavior is studied across time, identity, trauma, opportunity, and social location."}]}, {"id": "da4e733b-c2ea-4b1a-9ad1-5a367f37e344", "type": "topic", "title": "Generalist Practice Across Micro, Mezzo, and Macro Levels", "description": "This section explains the generalist model and how social workers move between direct practice, group work, organizations, communities, and policy action.", "children": [{"id": "78214c93-94f1-407f-92ad-26388535411a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Generalist practice model", "children": [{"id": "202d3542-101a-41b7-afdf-8364d6253299", "type": "concept", "title": "Engagement, assessment, planning, intervention, evaluation, and termination"}, {"id": "bd195427-f2b7-4dd5-9228-37253359df67", "type": "concept", "title": "Strengths perspective"}, {"id": "6adc5862-b0ba-4963-bd09-7884206344b2", "type": "concept", "title": "Evidence-informed decision-making"}, {"id": "013e846c-7eaa-4fd4-8913-c0f507e19109", "type": "concept", "title": "Ethical reflection throughout practice"}], "description": "Generalist practice teaches students to work flexibly across levels while using a common process."}, {"id": "11642f67-a158-49ba-8521-85d335377d3e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Micro, mezzo, and macro practice", "children": [{"id": "3ee6d617-d40e-45b9-b78f-db20983071d9", "type": "concept", "title": "Individuals and families"}, {"id": "db80ebf7-77c5-4ac7-bfcb-a046a78b8b51", "type": "concept", "title": "Groups and teams"}, {"id": "d4c3c104-21dc-412d-91cc-1e3d84b54d50", "type": "concept", "title": "Organizations and service systems"}, {"id": "58b66bb7-1318-4111-b4f9-0c7de335b980", "type": "concept", "title": "Communities, coalitions, and policy advocacy"}], "description": "Students learn that individual concerns are tied to families, groups, agencies, communities, and policy conditions."}, {"id": "d7d15fcc-8925-4096-9a70-dbdadaf9856d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Planned change and professional use of self", "children": [{"id": "6d694731-e2d5-412e-ab71-778c6aac0a5e", "type": "concept", "title": "Collaborative goal setting"}, {"id": "88288aec-a689-4a44-9ad8-62acb912b9e6", "type": "concept", "title": "Professional boundaries and self-awareness"}, {"id": "6e738164-b3fd-43b0-84ab-03f10838e2d1", "type": "concept", "title": "Documentation and supervision"}, {"id": "87e77f0d-70d7-4321-b600-5bbcd3c3cff7", "type": "concept", "title": "Evaluation of progress and outcomes"}], "description": "The planned change process turns good intentions into accountable practice."}]}, {"id": "6e7d37a6-1a89-46b8-9fe1-6302b9eb8240", "type": "topic", "title": "Ethics, Boundaries, Confidentiality, and Professional Judgment", "description": "Students learn that social work is not only caring work; it is accountable professional practice guided by ethical duties and difficult judgment calls.", "children": [{"id": "f66f8701-b7e4-4d7d-ba18-cd4b9aa4ae24", "type": "subtopic", "title": "NASW Code of Ethics foundation", "children": [{"id": "ced841e6-eaf6-48b2-b1ec-56a4a9f6a661", "type": "concept", "title": "Core values and ethical principles"}, {"id": "df2fd109-0acf-4cf5-ab72-2c2e2624db28", "type": "concept", "title": "Responsibilities to clients, colleagues, agencies, the profession, and society"}, {"id": "f2e0acda-4700-43e2-ab16-6c87995c2ef9", "type": "concept", "title": "Conflicts among values"}, {"id": "427ab8ab-0d10-424f-ac10-6ec3d5874d37", "type": "concept", "title": "Ethical decision-making models"}], "description": "Students learn to use ethics as a practical decision framework, not a decorative statement of ideals."}, {"id": "ee5b2df9-0943-4a33-942a-042d814fd4a4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Confidentiality, consent, and mandated duties", "children": [{"id": "1a2bbac5-06c8-464d-992c-6b094da042c0", "type": "concept", "title": "Informed consent"}, {"id": "03c11ea0-eddb-4a82-bafe-dfecfa15b06a", "type": "concept", "title": "Privacy and records"}, {"id": "83a2c3d4-e023-42dc-84e9-c94e4cfb69bb", "type": "concept", "title": "Mandated reporting and duty to protect"}, {"id": "076e3e3f-331e-42ce-baa0-745261748550", "type": "concept", "title": "Limits of confidentiality"}], "description": "This subtopic introduces duties that shape trust, safety, legal compliance, and client rights."}, {"id": "8a4cd42f-40a3-4734-916d-183d84d6df60", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Boundaries and professional judgment", "children": [{"id": "0f22bf4d-f213-4b17-b878-993d6a22fc20", "type": "concept", "title": "Dual relationships and conflicts of interest"}, {"id": "b3de13bf-61fd-4bff-a23f-1eae737473dc", "type": "concept", "title": "Self-disclosure and professional use of self"}, {"id": "e8bebeba-740f-4ec6-bb27-95e5db70df30", "type": "concept", "title": "Digital boundaries and social media"}, {"id": "8581c05e-ff9c-4fde-8904-d81ce54bb56e", "type": "concept", "title": "Supervision, consultation, and documentation"}], "description": "Beginning social workers need language for role clarity, power, dual relationships, and reflective practice."}]}, {"id": "5eba063c-f0aa-42bd-b850-72690fa4f1e7", "type": "topic", "title": "Diversity, Cultural Humility, and Anti-Oppressive Practice", "description": "This topic develops a foundation for culturally responsive, anti-racist, anti-oppressive, and identity-aware practice.", "children": [{"id": "a5b8b19b-e1f5-464f-9431-21cac0c3d63e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Cultural humility and responsiveness", "children": [{"id": "806214fd-79fd-4095-a8b2-ad922f547839", "type": "concept", "title": "Humility versus competence"}, {"id": "938ffea1-1c85-48e4-8bff-3482fdbeabff", "type": "concept", "title": "Reflexivity and positionality"}, {"id": "f5fa37c6-291f-4262-857f-b8c75f792a0d", "type": "concept", "title": "Language access and interpretation"}, {"id": "735594d8-8d59-4f54-82b6-d964ff4d6373", "type": "concept", "title": "Client-defined meaning and culturally grounded strengths"}], "description": "Students learn that effective practice requires lifelong learning, accountability, and attention to power."}, {"id": "c52de593-5ba9-4a98-9fff-e4157c912d88", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Identity, oppression, and intersectionality", "children": [{"id": "bcc07a93-c853-4904-99cf-ff083a8fa9cc", "type": "concept", "title": "Race, ethnicity, gender, sexuality, class, age, disability, religion, nationality, and immigration status"}, {"id": "b1183117-eb3b-46de-b814-a033bd4a4e56", "type": "concept", "title": "Intersectionality"}, {"id": "768e793f-1182-4f32-9bd3-efb111468f46", "type": "concept", "title": "Microaggressions and implicit bias"}, {"id": "a5c37ca4-1d47-4899-9b07-fea7ef617fcd", "type": "concept", "title": "Privilege, oppression, and structural inequality"}], "description": "This subtopic helps students understand how identities and systems interact in lived experience."}, {"id": "59fa35e4-afc5-45e2-827b-cb1cb12d3a17", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Anti-racist and anti-oppressive practice", "children": [{"id": "6d93a301-0935-4b2b-b7de-7e942a96d588", "type": "concept", "title": "Power analysis"}, {"id": "901a6b8f-5482-41fc-bb8f-914e4952660c", "type": "concept", "title": "Decolonizing and anti-racist practice commitments"}, {"id": "ae9950f2-9996-42f5-961c-caed9105eced", "type": "concept", "title": "Affirming LGBTQIA+ and disability justice practice"}, {"id": "ba6c55bd-2704-48ec-8609-91b8f5b007fb", "type": "concept", "title": "Allyship, solidarity, and accountability"}], "description": "Students learn to move from awareness to practice behaviors that reduce harm and support liberation."}]}, {"id": "9a86035c-3e24-42d3-8399-0b26cba3fea8", "type": "topic", "title": "Human Rights, Social Justice, Advocacy, and Power", "description": "Students connect individual helping roles to structural change, human rights, social justice, and advocacy responsibilities.", "children": [{"id": "48294e25-cfc2-4a19-b9cb-ebb8aea4a24c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Social justice as professional responsibility", "children": [{"id": "d935dc0e-744d-4f9a-a1bc-d28567c9758f", "type": "concept", "title": "Human rights frameworks"}, {"id": "d37ddd54-eec6-435b-9c0c-2d023f190180", "type": "concept", "title": "Economic and social justice"}, {"id": "3503200c-4678-4ab0-b56f-1fe15f3748ef", "type": "concept", "title": "Environmental justice and community wellbeing"}, {"id": "eaf1cf8f-a9a3-4569-9d42-395b759b88de", "type": "concept", "title": "Professional responsibility to challenge injustice"}], "description": "Students connect social work to changing unjust conditions, not only helping people survive them."}, {"id": "05f965ff-6f0a-4c28-be71-8bf6aa14f8c7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Power and structural analysis", "children": [{"id": "eb1f47a1-431e-4f80-a3bf-7a50cd9d853d", "type": "concept", "title": "Institutional power"}, {"id": "f1b6e754-70ff-4667-b2e0-16a66480a7e7", "type": "concept", "title": "Policy and administrative discretion"}, {"id": "9018f9ad-3ee1-4adb-9c44-0ab6b8bd2473", "type": "concept", "title": "Stigma, surveillance, and coercion"}, {"id": "17a3bc49-105a-4a1f-86f6-37c588ffe84d", "type": "concept", "title": "Community power and lived expertise"}], "description": "This subtopic teaches students to ask who benefits, who is harmed, and who decides."}, {"id": "ddcbaf24-6cd6-4189-9f50-97c32544e08b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Introductory advocacy roles", "children": [{"id": "246a0087-665a-4ef1-86cf-bca1f083d6b7", "type": "concept", "title": "Case advocacy"}, {"id": "85fe244a-346c-44fe-9400-edc5607e6014", "type": "concept", "title": "Legislative advocacy"}, {"id": "c8818586-d6ea-46da-a725-a169e1e95556", "type": "concept", "title": "Coalition work"}, {"id": "386ae626-4600-4579-823b-28021b1f8134", "type": "concept", "title": "Ethical storytelling and client consent"}], "description": "Students learn the first tools of policy and systems change."}]}, {"id": "551690e8-815d-46ca-a510-51eba0a843b3", "type": "topic", "title": "Social Welfare Systems, Policy, and Public Benefits", "description": "This section introduces the major social welfare systems that organize access to income, health care, food, housing, family support, and services.", "children": [{"id": "bc7ddec5-632f-4ddc-a51a-96750b39838c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Social welfare system overview", "children": [{"id": "25621ca5-632d-4fbe-a7ed-c66b651903d2", "type": "concept", "title": "Public assistance and social insurance"}, {"id": "5ed91aa5-afe0-442e-9716-6b657d4e35d8", "type": "concept", "title": "Federal, state, local, tribal, and nonprofit roles"}, {"id": "6d422411-9b60-476f-a88e-fe5b04a671a8", "type": "concept", "title": "Eligibility and enrollment"}, {"id": "6602180c-9b46-4f77-819f-4861672f974a", "type": "concept", "title": "Rights, entitlements, block grants, and discretionary programs"}], "description": "Students learn the basic map of U.S. social welfare supports and service systems."}, {"id": "c5cbba8c-356b-43e8-8f0e-7a7d89ec0abf", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Major benefits and services", "children": [{"id": "c96f563f-9e1b-46df-8e54-12ab6e671888", "type": "concept", "title": "TANF, Social Security, SSI, SSDI"}, {"id": "7f289b72-661a-4a66-b04c-295f36ea849d", "type": "concept", "title": "Medicaid, Medicare, and behavioral health services"}, {"id": "9ea94d26-c657-4e41-a9bd-5490ffcf3320", "type": "concept", "title": "SNAP, WIC, school meals, housing assistance, and homelessness services"}, {"id": "9c3cbe82-159e-412b-9767-c294754040fb", "type": "concept", "title": "Child welfare, aging, disability, and family support services"}], "description": "This subtopic builds enough literacy for students to understand common referral and policy contexts."}, {"id": "ed6e99aa-b1bc-4dbb-9144-f744e5492e9e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Policy-practice connection", "children": [{"id": "cefe4fb9-3872-47c9-89a2-4acaf22a17d5", "type": "concept", "title": "Benefit cliffs"}, {"id": "9d47ac3c-053a-4447-8bc5-a91aeead2951", "type": "concept", "title": "Administrative burden"}, {"id": "f730edb0-834d-4767-a348-c44ee0075e44", "type": "concept", "title": "Stigma and access barriers"}, {"id": "6d01fba5-aed7-42a3-a0f9-6116744285d9", "type": "concept", "title": "Policy analysis questions for beginners"}], "description": "Students see how rules, budgets, and administrative design shape everyday practice."}]}, {"id": "85078e2f-f5a9-4241-9a5f-089aa6762e19", "type": "topic", "title": "Fields of Practice and Populations Served", "description": "Students survey where social workers practice and how settings shape roles, populations, risks, strengths, and interventions.", "children": [{"id": "08c150a1-08ce-41dd-a029-3b05fa890244", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Major practice fields", "children": [{"id": "82fbebd4-82b9-4a4b-8def-e547e7aa9dab", "type": "concept", "title": "Child welfare and family services"}, {"id": "2e652d28-c15b-41b3-8d34-5c26ba2bfb0a", "type": "concept", "title": "Schools and youth development"}, {"id": "83906451-ef1c-4c4b-8f69-020798dc3c3d", "type": "concept", "title": "Health, mental health, and substance use"}, {"id": "40365d05-c022-4766-9719-f8a74f3ee557", "type": "concept", "title": "Aging, disability, housing, justice, military, immigrants and refugees"}], "description": "Students survey the breadth of social work and begin identifying areas they may want to explore."}, {"id": "1e41d066-a76f-4c35-95ed-149b68a45b85", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Population-specific practice awareness", "children": [{"id": "0ee71c38-11b1-42ec-a479-8befc351201b", "type": "concept", "title": "Children, youth, and families"}, {"id": "45cd9942-adbc-49fb-93e5-53cdca12e52c", "type": "concept", "title": "Older adults and caregivers"}, {"id": "db1e89aa-e7d4-4c95-8f47-6906a35f782b", "type": "concept", "title": "LGBTQIA+ and gender-diverse communities"}, {"id": "5ec5075c-348d-489a-b5d4-65682a33ba15", "type": "concept", "title": "Immigrant, refugee, rural, Indigenous, and historically marginalized communities"}], "description": "A strong introduction teaches students to avoid stereotypes while noticing population-specific histories and service barriers."}, {"id": "089fbc37-6528-4b2d-9449-843959ad9f2c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Role fit and setting constraints", "children": [{"id": "beeb92cb-6522-4262-9b60-b6161b705e97", "type": "concept", "title": "Voluntary, court-ordered, and mandated services"}, {"id": "e17b3246-7963-411c-b824-6d1aea99efe2", "type": "concept", "title": "Agency policies and service eligibility"}, {"id": "efc9450d-194a-49c7-8068-71a10f018aa9", "type": "concept", "title": "Interdisciplinary settings"}, {"id": "38efeea8-e22e-416f-bd26-bf39eb191e6f", "type": "concept", "title": "Safety, risk, and rights"}], "description": "Students learn that social work roles change depending on agency mission, law, funding, and client status."}]}, {"id": "f2d90336-2164-4d24-a6c4-ebbe8c442748", "type": "topic", "title": "Engagement, Communication, and the Helping Relationship", "description": "This topic introduces the practical skills used to build trust, listen well, ask useful questions, and collaborate with clients and communities.", "children": [{"id": "8edf2e57-22e0-47be-bcca-ac502ecaa6c2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Engagement and rapport", "children": [{"id": "bb04fc7d-4c9e-4d00-b0fa-920435d95736", "type": "concept", "title": "Warmth, empathy, genuineness, and respect"}, {"id": "3641cc12-6f0d-4cb6-bd75-367d9d235c77", "type": "concept", "title": "Role explanation and informed consent"}, {"id": "e23b3cbc-bd50-40f2-b355-802f2c691106", "type": "concept", "title": "Working with ambivalence or mistrust"}, {"id": "cc20ffc1-239b-4cff-abed-d824d5c16b72", "type": "concept", "title": "Engagement across difference and power"}], "description": "Students learn that change work starts with trust, respect, clarity, and collaborative purpose."}, {"id": "833e9590-cb3c-4778-bddc-af5772dee471", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Interviewing and listening skills", "children": [{"id": "c10d2bdd-d66d-4608-af7a-c70e548d54eb", "type": "concept", "title": "Open and closed questions"}, {"id": "c61783b5-0789-4f98-a76d-a8d72616656a", "type": "concept", "title": "Reflection, summarizing, and validation"}, {"id": "578aca0f-7c4f-4733-a317-25409b5652d5", "type": "concept", "title": "Silence, pacing, and nonverbal communication"}, {"id": "fbed8df1-e279-4862-9caf-e8d33a6210ab", "type": "concept", "title": "Motivational interviewing basics"}], "description": "This subtopic introduces concrete communication behaviors that support ethical assessment and collaboration."}, {"id": "f3fdd3ee-95bf-4fc2-82da-e2d87ba6f543", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Difficult conversations", "children": [{"id": "3b4a8384-17a5-495c-af2a-50eae11a6762", "type": "concept", "title": "De-escalation basics"}, {"id": "c71beff4-4118-4b6b-a1cf-d84cedc87a76", "type": "concept", "title": "Responding to anger or grief"}, {"id": "6a3fd4dc-ddfa-46c6-9251-5c1561490ad1", "type": "concept", "title": "Repairing ruptures"}, {"id": "2c6610ce-285a-45d4-8e99-f97f5a41a831", "type": "concept", "title": "Maintaining boundaries while showing care"}], "description": "Students practice communication in moments involving conflict, distress, risk, shame, or disagreement."}]}, {"id": "7d8d3696-52c5-4853-b97e-94a26e6cc0eb", "type": "topic", "title": "Assessment, Strengths, Case Management, and Resource Navigation", "description": "Students learn how social workers understand needs and strengths, coordinate services, and help people navigate complex systems.", "children": [{"id": "b0ac659b-f278-4229-bbaf-45b855fbe4b0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Introductory assessment", "children": [{"id": "3c42d1e8-b191-468d-8083-8331e869a33c", "type": "concept", "title": "Biopsychosocial-spiritual assessment"}, {"id": "e8ff8cbd-e6f1-4843-8283-2d3dc22e5529", "type": "concept", "title": "Strengths, needs, risks, and protective factors"}, {"id": "314073ca-cf07-4175-bf84-3f061fb3eb59", "type": "concept", "title": "Family, community, and policy context"}, {"id": "cee5da6f-f240-4d6b-b27a-5620a61bef5a", "type": "concept", "title": "Client goals and priorities"}], "description": "Assessment is framed as collaborative understanding rather than diagnosis from a distance."}, {"id": "456ccd16-2513-4651-848e-40cdcef12141", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Case management and service coordination", "children": [{"id": "1ac0cd41-e2cf-4d81-a309-cab2ea12630e", "type": "concept", "title": "Resource mapping"}, {"id": "25aed83d-8418-4663-8c29-3ee345fd7145", "type": "concept", "title": "Eligibility and referral pathways"}, {"id": "8a1b68fb-4c15-438a-9111-c1fc49e2b796", "type": "concept", "title": "Warm handoffs and follow-up"}, {"id": "0f2bb18e-2d5f-46b9-974d-6a23c0a84d64", "type": "concept", "title": "Interagency communication and consent"}], "description": "Students learn how social workers help people move through fragmented systems."}, {"id": "bcc3f4c0-07ba-4090-89bc-60467175e49b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Documentation and accountability", "children": [{"id": "8631bf8e-7b12-44c4-bf25-db485a683815", "type": "concept", "title": "Progress notes and case summaries"}, {"id": "05fbb1a9-9692-44eb-bb2a-4a112bc872b9", "type": "concept", "title": "Objective versus interpretive language"}, {"id": "7c3df1f9-8107-4464-88fe-ed68c088ccb2", "type": "concept", "title": "Confidentiality and records"}, {"id": "806d9803-ead8-430b-bdb7-a397993f0fe8", "type": "concept", "title": "Outcome tracking and supervision use"}], "description": "Beginning students learn that good documentation protects continuity, ethics, learning, and client rights."}]}, {"id": "62642229-3149-4c9a-90de-231d535ff55d", "type": "topic", "title": "Evidence-Informed Practice, Research Literacy, and Evaluation", "description": "This section builds the beginner research literacy needed to distinguish evidence, values, context, and professional judgment.", "children": [{"id": "9a69e360-0393-4d3c-bfee-ba61c950fc99", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Evidence-informed practice", "children": [{"id": "b123bb16-dedf-4a90-bb62-60345cb1fde8", "type": "concept", "title": "Evidence-based and evidence-informed practice"}, {"id": "7f82cbe9-38ad-4111-976c-7f6a3c28bc05", "type": "concept", "title": "Practice wisdom and lived experience"}, {"id": "b4911ed0-1c5c-43bd-bb68-bd8e25b365fe", "type": "concept", "title": "Fit, feasibility, and adaptation"}, {"id": "d1d055f5-d7c5-450e-87a5-8133d86ca592", "type": "concept", "title": "Harms of one-size-fits-all evidence use"}], "description": "Students learn to combine research evidence, client values, cultural context, and practitioner expertise."}, {"id": "dc4e76a1-2099-43dc-83f9-78f0ded5b1c2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Research literacy for beginners", "children": [{"id": "80cb7352-6887-4ee8-87b0-8e2e4b912654", "type": "concept", "title": "Quantitative, qualitative, and mixed methods"}, {"id": "b4af2973-8afd-483b-8be9-9d42a6b64743", "type": "concept", "title": "Sampling and measurement basics"}, {"id": "0f19f6d0-9915-4e2a-8821-3f586b27ba4b", "type": "concept", "title": "Program evaluation"}, {"id": "3ba22f7b-7537-4fae-ac6a-a08070a410fd", "type": "concept", "title": "Ethics and human subjects protections"}], "description": "This subtopic prepares students to read claims with curiosity and healthy skepticism."}, {"id": "932f9a54-2f45-4894-b91c-cdfe989e6179", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Using data for learning and justice", "children": [{"id": "91a85593-eea0-41a2-b86d-30fa86f80a86", "type": "concept", "title": "Outcome measures"}, {"id": "9af6f340-c234-41a2-b16f-45fe61210c3c", "type": "concept", "title": "Disaggregated data"}, {"id": "84abcbfa-d899-4367-a092-d767143ea996", "type": "concept", "title": "Data privacy and consent"}, {"id": "5c4c0c89-31a2-4ea5-82fa-4a78835fb515", "type": "concept", "title": "Community accountability and interpretation"}], "description": "Students learn that data can reveal inequity but can also reproduce bias if used uncritically."}]}, {"id": "304ea1ca-209d-4af3-a254-1447f8a65dfe", "type": "topic", "title": "Trauma-Informed, Resilience-Oriented, and Crisis-Aware Practice", "description": "Students learn introductory principles for recognizing trauma, supporting safety, and avoiding practices that intensify harm.", "children": [{"id": "bc709c80-c40d-4113-b9ab-b7000e48ef48", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Trauma-informed principles", "children": [{"id": "4fe8c5d2-6179-4a88-8ecb-a8e54933bb9a", "type": "concept", "title": "Safety, trustworthiness, choice, collaboration, and empowerment"}, {"id": "0ae1c93c-bdc5-48db-9aa6-4e4c2d472302", "type": "concept", "title": "Cultural, historical, and gender considerations"}, {"id": "b47be955-5d7a-432e-a106-277fdcc0c48f", "type": "concept", "title": "Avoiding retraumatization"}, {"id": "f8ed39fc-225b-4f0e-841b-febd4aa89ce9", "type": "concept", "title": "Universal precautions in service settings"}], "description": "Students learn introductory principles for recognizing trauma and reducing avoidable harm."}, {"id": "d2976d24-0140-4e6d-a05a-55d12ae0925c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Resilience and protective factors", "children": [{"id": "213ab919-1125-4844-9911-3146e066d5b9", "type": "concept", "title": "Individual and relational resilience"}, {"id": "8b5b15d0-246f-4c65-a636-43eb0302a49b", "type": "concept", "title": "Family and community supports"}, {"id": "83a60502-6ff7-4b4e-8c22-f4df640823c8", "type": "concept", "title": "Meaning-making and culture"}, {"id": "7a7fe8ed-2c55-49ed-b69d-9d95b5619c7d", "type": "concept", "title": "Post-traumatic growth cautions and limits"}], "description": "This subtopic balances trauma awareness with strengths, relationships, community, and possibility."}, {"id": "f51c929f-1610-44d5-b7fc-5402a422315d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Crisis awareness and referral", "children": [{"id": "8fab81e4-e354-4555-90e7-2afdae168d39", "type": "concept", "title": "Risk and safety signals"}, {"id": "05071f50-162f-4c5d-8e56-58ad7b810068", "type": "concept", "title": "Suicide and violence referral pathways"}, {"id": "793c85b2-9c39-4e5e-9b7d-b52b145bdfc0", "type": "concept", "title": "Crisis de-escalation basics"}, {"id": "9a326a29-3b9b-43f4-949d-874dbbbd760d", "type": "concept", "title": "Supervision, emergency protocols, and scope limits"}], "description": "Students learn what beginners should notice and how to seek support rather than act beyond competence."}]}, {"id": "b0e238de-8e28-4d7c-a064-a451d1069936", "type": "topic", "title": "Organizations, Interprofessional Teams, and Community Practice", "description": "This topic introduces social work inside agencies, schools, hospitals, courts, nonprofits, community organizations, and interdisciplinary teams.", "children": [{"id": "8beb49a3-f5f8-4dbb-ac81-cebae55266ef", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Agency-based practice", "children": [{"id": "429628af-ad4d-4831-aa4f-9d2a517cdc8b", "type": "concept", "title": "Public and nonprofit organizations"}, {"id": "2f46f114-0354-4bf2-b439-d64145dd6b82", "type": "concept", "title": "Supervision and hierarchy"}, {"id": "51251800-fb2f-4518-9dbb-e52631d9d54d", "type": "concept", "title": "Workload, burnout, and self-care"}, {"id": "a699d8b0-026d-4963-9690-d5a840a21a86", "type": "concept", "title": "Ethical tensions inside agencies"}], "description": "Students learn how agencies shape social work through mission, funding, rules, caseloads, and accountability."}, {"id": "2fe0914c-0685-4494-8c1e-f7a9cf87b055", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Interprofessional collaboration", "children": [{"id": "a9d0dd4c-060a-4661-809f-34d873ee8a86", "type": "concept", "title": "Health, education, legal, behavioral health, and justice teams"}, {"id": "b03401d9-cbbf-4762-a229-74943d92f130", "type": "concept", "title": "Communication across professional cultures"}, {"id": "1a88f214-41b9-43a3-8de7-e00b2f18bac7", "type": "concept", "title": "Confidentiality and releases"}, {"id": "ce1c7f31-48fb-41c4-a0c9-1554bf8c0ca5", "type": "concept", "title": "Team conflict and client advocacy"}], "description": "Social workers often practice in teams, so students learn the basics of role clarity and collaboration."}, {"id": "d19fc70b-e759-4902-bd22-dcf21ed491e6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Community and macro practice", "children": [{"id": "38c69cb2-9190-4797-b4dd-6e0d6be7c346", "type": "concept", "title": "Community needs and assets"}, {"id": "6bd10991-b042-4ee0-8f65-d192159f6b9d", "type": "concept", "title": "Coalitions and organizing"}, {"id": "2bfa332e-22ec-4a41-b926-c231cbca7c81", "type": "concept", "title": "Group facilitation"}, {"id": "bf22147d-a4c4-49ae-9f81-76c2d64fede3", "type": "concept", "title": "Policy and systems change projects"}], "description": "Students see community work as core social work rather than an optional add-on."}]}, {"id": "270462d4-bd6c-493a-85fe-e3bdd388307f", "type": "topic", "title": "Education, Field Learning, Licensure, Careers, and Professional Identity", "description": "Students map the pathway from introductory coursework to field education, credentials, supervision, licensure, and lifelong professional growth.", "children": [{"id": "bfcf7b27-a245-4da7-a943-2bb8dd18dfa5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Social work education pathway", "children": [{"id": "3ace8cb3-0f7a-4b14-9207-67f468bffe49", "type": "concept", "title": "BSW, MSW, advanced standing, and doctoral pathways"}, {"id": "53643870-d08f-47f5-8c0b-efde9e6331c8", "type": "concept", "title": "CSWE accreditation"}, {"id": "84ce8288-23bf-4999-be19-48ebaafe6d5b", "type": "concept", "title": "Generalist and specialized curricula"}, {"id": "9ea69bc3-ad14-4d84-87bb-c791bee6ec50", "type": "concept", "title": "Field education as signature pedagogy"}], "description": "Students map how introductory coursework leads into competency-based education and field learning."}, {"id": "27c9dc5c-9e1e-466c-a874-c207389324f6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Licensure and professional regulation", "children": [{"id": "e1ba05f5-8caf-4d54-be59-1851b279382d", "type": "concept", "title": "ASWB exam context"}, {"id": "d6511b4b-a11a-4ba7-83ac-17642ea1e163", "type": "concept", "title": "LBSW, LMSW, LCSW, and jurisdictional variation"}, {"id": "7aaf011c-549a-4dd2-b0e0-164aa29a1099", "type": "concept", "title": "Supervision requirements"}, {"id": "b5af05c9-15a5-45ea-9a2e-4ec072716fc2", "type": "concept", "title": "Continuing education and ethics"}], "description": "This subtopic gives a beginner-friendly overview without pretending licensure is the same in every jurisdiction."}, {"id": "888018c6-7363-4058-bbc3-3db14aba6101", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Careers and professional sustainability", "children": [{"id": "21a446ef-341c-4760-82e5-ce1304d67e8e", "type": "concept", "title": "Career settings and labor outlook"}, {"id": "5554ec94-1779-4f3a-9f61-7ed6572d7b1e", "type": "concept", "title": "Supervision and mentorship"}, {"id": "7681d531-46ee-429c-afc2-d05d37bb77bd", "type": "concept", "title": "Professional associations"}, {"id": "eb207d4d-5305-4ac4-b9f0-08aedeb53bba", "type": "concept", "title": "Burnout, moral distress, and reflective self-care"}], "description": "Students explore possible careers while learning that social work requires reflective practice and care for one's own sustainability."}]}, {"id": "0af5ff81-0025-4ee3-a1d1-8c32120a58f3", "type": "topic", "title": "Capstone: Social Work Field Exploration and Reflective Practice Portfolio", "description": "The course culminates in a field-of-practice exploration that integrates values, policy, ethics, evidence, population context, and professional reflection.", "children": [{"id": "e89e0fc8-2108-4f1b-9ebd-f725c66c7704", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Field-of-practice exploration", "children": [{"id": "e103fce0-30d5-4acf-89a8-5a10f09afc8e", "type": "concept", "title": "Agency or field profile"}, {"id": "298fed20-ea05-4189-b4d2-df73c0c6c373", "type": "concept", "title": "Population served and community context"}, {"id": "f52efa79-002e-4240-85cf-954b8dbe0500", "type": "concept", "title": "Social worker roles and interdisciplinary partners"}, {"id": "09bbc752-39d0-430e-9060-c494b3b2732d", "type": "concept", "title": "Key policy and funding conditions"}], "description": "Students synthesize the course by choosing one practice field and studying it through roles, populations, policy, ethics, and evidence."}, {"id": "672f7ed6-31b5-48a4-9512-b5dcfd618a28", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Values, ethics, and justice analysis", "children": [{"id": "0e32de5f-748f-4e56-8772-1d8537d7f5a0", "type": "concept", "title": "Ethical dilemma identification"}, {"id": "1aabf758-d94e-44ec-9e4f-e219ca8579e6", "type": "concept", "title": "Power and oppression analysis"}, {"id": "1a119232-653b-4b1e-abbf-e181cb92485f", "type": "concept", "title": "Client rights and self-determination"}, {"id": "fc753aa0-ae5a-4b6f-bdb9-a74573c0a172", "type": "concept", "title": "Advocacy opportunity"}], "description": "The capstone asks students to connect professional values to real tensions in practice."}, {"id": "f081f75f-e645-4be8-a649-00848ef0ac1b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Reflective professional portfolio", "children": [{"id": "3b8e596d-4613-42aa-93e8-1d37b2112c1f", "type": "concept", "title": "Professional identity reflection"}, {"id": "4efbc529-531a-4fb9-b413-aa28dda97abf", "type": "concept", "title": "Skills to develop before field placement"}, {"id": "096e1dda-6d83-48fc-b5cb-6026808b5da3", "type": "concept", "title": "Resource list and career pathway"}, {"id": "d373fff5-472b-4cba-bdd7-1c8f1e7971bc", "type": "concept", "title": "Learning goals for future coursework"}], "description": "Students end with a grounded statement of learning, questions, and next steps."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$iswjson$::jsonb,
  true,
  false,
  'course',
